1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Hawcê ye. Dara Ne'cîkê ye,
 
It is Hawcê. It is the Ne'cîk tree,

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Dara gelekî kevnar e, Ne'cîkê dihatin vir.
 
It's a very ancient tree, Ne'cîk would come here.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Bi dewar dihatin, av dibirin...
 
They came with cattle, and took water...

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Û ev gelî jî hemî bi vê bîrê tê naskirin.
 
And this entire valley is known by this well.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Bi hemî bi vê bîrê tê naskirin. Geliyê Bîrê.
 
All of it is known by this well. The Well Valley.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Ev bîra kê ve ne?
 
Who does this well belong to?

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Ev bîra Romaniyan e.
 
This is the Romans' well.

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Omrê xwe pir dirêj e. Kes nizane ji çi wextî da ye.
 
Its age is very long. No one knows from what time it is.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Bes, Romiyan... Berî Selahedîn bû. Selahedîn jî 1300 sal
e...
 
But, the Romans... It was before Saladin. Saladin is also
1300 years...

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Vê bîrê û vê dara çinarê ve, 1300 sal teqrîben heye yanî.
 
With this well and this sycamore tree, it is roughly 1300
years old.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Berê ji ev cihê kurda ye, piştî wî...
 
Previously this was a Kurdish place, after that...

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Ev cihê kurda ye, tebî. Yanî beriya romiyan jî kurd bûn. Li
romiyan re jî kurd in.
 
This is a Kurdish place, of course. That is, even before the
Romans it was Kurdish. And after the Romans, it is Kurdish.

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Belê. Na tu behsa dara kir, ev dar a çinarê ye?
 
Yes. Now you talked about the tree, is this tree a sycamore
tree?

14
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Çinar e.
 
It is a sycamore.

15
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Te got emrê wê çiqas e ye?
 
You said how old is it?

16
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
1300 sal e.
 
It is 1300 years old.

17
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Min dît rojek nivîsandibû tine, yanî kesî lêkolînek
çêkiriye?
 
I saw one day it wasn't written anywhere, I mean, has anyone
done a research?

18
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Na, bi devkî gotin.
 
No, it was said orally.

19
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Bi devkî hatine gotin, hatine gotin.
 
It has been said orally, it has been said.

20
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Ev dar a jî çiqas wê bilindbûna wê heye?
 
And how much is the height of this tree?

21
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Qala bilindbûna wê teqrîben pencî metir bilindbûn zêde hebû.
 
Its height was probably more than fifty meters tall.

22
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Bes, milet hat qus kir, kirin êzing... aah.. dar qus kirine.
 
But, people came and cut it down, made firewood... aah..
they cut the tree.

23
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Dar pir mezin bû.
 
The tree was very big.

24
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Dîbê berê jî, golek... Çî ko koka darê ra, golek derbas
dibe...
 
They say in the past, a pond... A pond passes through the
root of the tree...

25
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Koka darê ra.
 
Through the root of the tree.

26
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Naha zelal... me halê darê vîda, belî yanî halekî hîn
vekiriye.
 
Now it's clear... we saw the condition of the tree, it is
evident that it has opened up more.

27
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Na, ev kelek... dar a çî ye? Ev mehser e ye?
 
Now, this structure... what is this piece of wood? Is it an
olive press?

28
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Haho mekbes e. Zemçî çêdikiribû paşê jî... girtin...
 
That is a press. They used to make zemçî, and then... they
closed it...

29
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Mehser e ye.
 
It is an olive press.

30
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Mamoste, de him, te go, di weşqe vê bîrê tine ne?
 
Teacher, you said, there's nothing else like this well?

31
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Tine ye, na. Heye, tê ne...
 
There isn't, no. There is, they come...

32
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Av jî niha têda heye?
 
Is there water in it now?

33
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Tê jî av.
 
Water comes into it.

34
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Ava wê qe kuhişk nabe.
 
Its water never dries up.

35
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Û biharê av diçele da derdibe...
 
And in spring, the water overflows...

36
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Heta biharê meha şeşan... meha pêncan, şeşan, dimîne
diheştebe.
 
Until spring, the sixth month... the fifth month, the sixth,
it stays until it dries up.

37
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Ne heştebe, ava kaniyê qut dibe.
 
When it doesn't dry up, the spring water gets cut off.

38
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Ava baranê ye yanê?
 
Is it rain water, you mean?

39
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Na ava baranê nakave.
 
No, rain water doesn't fall into it.

40
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Ava jê çat e, ji çiyê.
 
It's mountain water, from the mountain.

41
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Mala te ava be, sipas ji te ra.
 
Thank you, thanks to you.

42
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Mala te jî ava be, ser serê min, ser çavên min. Hatin a we
pir bi xêr hatine.
 
Thank you too, upon my head, upon my eyes. You are very
welcome.

43
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Sipas, saet xweş.
 
Thanks, bless you.

44
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Saeta te jî xweş, ehlen we sehlen. Ser serî...
 
Bless you too, welcome. Upon my head...

45
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Li biniya gundê Hawcê li rojavayê bîrek a ava heye...
 
Below the village of Hawcê, in the west, there is a water
well...

46
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
bi navê Bîra Alîcaratê naskirin.
 
Known by the name Bîra Alîcaratê.

47
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Xelkê herêmê gundan av jê dibirin...
 
The people of the region's villages took water from it...

48
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
û pezên xwe jî av didan...
 
and they also watered their sheep...

49
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,000
û ta naha...
 
and until now...

50
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
di hemî demsalan da ava xwe dimîne...
 
in all seasons, its water remains...

51
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:51,000
û di biharê da dibe cihê geşt û seyranê.
 
and in the spring, it becomes a place for outings and
picnics.

52
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Apê Xelîl, merheba ji te ra.
 
Uncle Xelîl, hello to you.

53
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Ehlan, merheba, ser çava. Hatin a we bi xêr be, ehlan we
sehlan.
 
Welcome, hello, upon my eyes. Welcome, you are very welcome.

54
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Saxbî. Apê Xelîl, te di her gundekî em digerên...
 
Be well. Uncle Xelîl, in every village we wander...

55
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
tiştekî wan yî balkêş ci hebe. Kasekî necar be... Yanî çi
kar di gund de hebe em çêdikin.
 
if they have anything interesting. If someone is a
carpenter... I mean, whatever work there is in the village,
we do it.

56
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Em derbas gundê we Hawcê caw bûn, behsa te kirin...
 
We passed by your village Hawcê, they talked about you...

57
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Ser serî min û ser çavê min re, sehet xweş be...
 
Upon my head and upon my eyes, bless you...

58
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Saxbî. Goti te necar e.
 
Be well. They said you are a carpenter.

59
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

60
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Me got em derbazbûn cem te bin.
 
We said we should stop by your place.

61
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Bi sed selaman hatin... Ser seran û ser çavan...
 
You've come with a hundred greetings... Upon my head and
eyes...

62
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Saxbe. Apê Xelîl, kîjan berê da tu bêjî... na, te çî çêdikî?
Ji berê da.
 
Be well. Uncle Xelîl, from what time in the past you say...
no, what do you make? From the past.

63
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Ji berê da... hevçaran çêdikim...
 
From the past... I make ploughs...

64
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Ez kîran çêdikim... ez... cencera, cencera çêdikim...
 
I make ploughshares... I... threshing sledges, I make
threshing sledges...

65
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
ji berê da, yanî min çêdikirin. Tê da zane... Ê ha...
 
from the past, I mean, I used to make them. You know... Like
that...

66
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
E tu ji kê e'limî û ji kê fêr bû?
 
And from whom did you learn, who taught you?

67
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Ez ji kesekî na e'limîm. Em binêrîne bûn, binêrîna na,
halîyan, ez çibinerim, ba kes... ji bê xwe da yekê we çêkim.
 
I didn't learn from anyone. We were observers, not
observation, currently, whatever I look at, without
anyone... from myself I'll make one like it.

68
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Ebeden. Ez kesê re ne e'limîm.
 
Never. I didn't learn from anyone.

69
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Bi gilkî em jê e'limîm.
 
I completely learned it by myself.

70
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Yanê di gund de, ji malbata te da, kes tine bû? Necar tine
bû?
 
Meaning in the village, from your family, there was no one?
There was no carpenter?

71
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Na, di aîla me da kes jî necar tine bû. Bes em.. binêrîne..
 
No, in our family there was no carpenter either. But we...
observe...

72
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Ya pê ye, tu çî dixwaze? Tu çi dixwaze ew e te çavê min e,
min çêdikirin...
 
And then, what do you want? What you want, it's upon my
eyes, I made them...

73
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Te bi xwe, ya pê xwa jî girt.
 
You yourself, you took it upon yourself.

74
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Ya pê xwe jî girt.
 
Took it upon myself.

75
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Her bijî, saet te xweş be.
 
Long live, bless you.

76
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Saet te jî, destê te xweş bîn.
 
Bless you too, bless your hands.

77
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Saxbe. Te go, te cencer çêdikirin...
 
Be well. You said you used to make threshing sledges...

78
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

79
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Naha, dibêjin cencer.. pirrani jî nemane.
 
Now, they say threshing sledges... mostly don't remain.

80
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Na, tu nîne, kê mane?
 
No, there are none, what remains?

81
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Ê cencer çend sal in, e nemane yanê? Beriya te bî çiqas derê
cencer bû?
 
How many years have threshing sledges not been around?
Before you, how many threshing sledges were there?

82
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Belkî pêncî sal, çil sal heye. Si û pênc çil heye. Nemane.
 
Maybe fifty years, forty years there are. Thirty-five, forty
there are. They don't remain.

83
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Derasat derketin... deh derketin.
 
Combine harvesters came out... ten came out.

84
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Ew da'we cencera... dera mir. Çi qas derbê me devêr, bar
dikirin,
 
The era of threshing sledges... died. Whenever we used to
thresh, we loaded,

85
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,000
me qatir dikirin, ev a... de me hev dikirin.. şixulê, bar
dikirin...
 
we used mules, these... we used to plow... work, we
loaded...

86
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:43,000
E xweşikbûna, berê gunda çiqas xweş bû dema ku ev serbê
dera... Bêhîvre kar... yanî gundî bi xwega bi hevra dibin
alîkar, bi hevra kar dikirin...
 
And the beauty, the past of the villages, how beautiful it
was when they threshed... With each other the work... I mean
the villagers helped each other, worked together...

87
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Cencera yekî xilasbû, me sele da bederek xwe xilasbûbû e
cîranîtî me derî ta xilas te ma, ne dihişt ta tûyê xwe belê
wê here.
 
When one's threshing sledge finished, we gave... when his
pile was finished, our neighborliness, we went until he
finished too, didn't let him stay until he went too.

88
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Na ta ke vir ve xar gindîk ro, ev gindî jî avakro, yanî hev
jî bixworo, rakro.
 
No, completely everything was ruined, this village was
ruined too, I mean they also ate each other, ruined.

89
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Yanî bi rastî, cencer tê bîra min jî. Ez biçûk bûm. Li gund
ro rûniştî bûm.
 
Honestly, I remember threshing sledges too. I was small. I
lived in the village.

90
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Yanî min dî, çawa cencer wî wextî xwe, dema xwe derbas
dikirin. Hem sitran jî di gotin...
 
I mean I saw how threshing sledges spent their time back
then. They also sang songs...

91
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
cîran bi hev ra dibin alîkar.
 
neighbors helped each other.

92
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Yanî xwaşîk bîn pir xwaş bû. E te din, te cencer te, bi xwe,
te çêdikir?
 
I mean, they were beautiful, very nice. And what else, you,
a threshing sledge, yourself, did you make it?

93
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Min cencer çêdikir başqe...
 
I made threshing sledges, what else...

94
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Yanî wek necarî te...
 
I mean like as a carpenter...

95
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Wekî necarî ez çê..., hevd... tişta çêdikim, dera çêdikim
weke çi çêdikim...
 
As a carpenter I make..., everything... I make things, I
make doors, what else I make...

96
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Apê Xelîl, dema tu çêdikî, te dîsa te livê ciyê çêdikî? Te
l'gund çêdikir?
 
Uncle Xelîl, when you made them, did you make them here in
this place? Did you make them in the village?

97
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Te l'ku derê çêdikir?
 
Where did you make them?

98
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Min li gund çêdikir. L'mald...
 
I made them in the village. At home...

99
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,000
L'maldê wek na...
 
At home like now...

100
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:37,000
L'malda diçêkir ez di çûma Cût. Ez Cût dihatim, sê çara
hevcara a hewce ne. Da ta zanê...
 
At home I made it, I used to go to Cût. I came from Cût,
three, four ploughs are needed. You know...

101
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
Weha tinne bûn.
 
They didn't exist like this.

102
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Tê Cût dikir?
 
You plowed?

103
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Lên min Cût dikir, ez Cût da hatim... hevcara jê şikiyo li
devê hewşê nebe çêkirona ovkirana, xudana xwe damne te
xwedan di birine.
 
Yes, I plowed, I came from plowing... his plough is broken,
at the door of the yard they would make it, fix it, their
owner would put it, you owner took it.

104
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Apê Xelîl, na, te dî, ta bihesa cût kir. Cewa jî hemî çiyane
û gelîne...
 
Uncle Xelîl, now, you saw, you talked about plowing. The
place is also all mountains and valleys...

105
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,000
e ev çi zehmetî te hebû?
 
and what difficulty did it have for you?

106
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Hey wî! zehmetê wê çaxê, zehmet pir bûn. Yanî radbûn pir
bûn. Ne wekî nakabû.
 
Oh wow! The difficulties of that time, difficulties were
many. I mean, getting up was a lot. Not like it is now.

107
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Naka alet bi derketin e av derketine nebet rat bi bî... Tu
rahet nabî...
 
Now equipment has come out, things have come out, there is
no need to get up... You will not be comfortable...

108
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Yanî çiqas zehmetî bû ev çala çava, bavêk me... kesên mezin
yên me ruspîyên me
 
I mean, how much difficulty were these holes, our fathers...
our elders, our white-beards

109
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Ev çalên gî va dan, wekirine, darên zeytûnê...
 
They dug all these holes, they made them, olive trees...

110
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Hevo kûpciyo wakir... kûbcî hatin.
 
The explosives made it... explosives came.

111
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Ji zemanê ku kobcî hati bi vî çî xetin u ge dir getin fedî
kirin gavawikirin, gavkirin.
 
From the time that explosives came, they went into this
place, and they took places, they opened up, they dug, they
did.

112
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Yanî ve dêmada gî zeytûn candîn...
 
I mean in this era they planted all olives...

113
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Elê paşê zeytûn candîn... dar candîn... aw..
 
Yes, then they planted olives... planted trees... oh..

114
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Yê çiqas zehmetbû yen...
 
And how difficult it was...

115
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:39,000
E zehmet, diwext çaxeda diraktor tin ebî ,dar tine bî ...
cûd bî cudê dewe bî ... e cût docotin...pir radbîn pir
bîn...
 
And difficult, at that time there were no tractors, no
trees... it was plowing, plowing with cattle... and plowing
they plowed... it was a lot of getting up, a lot...

116
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
ne wa ke ne ko bi .
 
not like how it is now.

117
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Bes xwekşe bî ne wîdemi xeş pî ne nha...
 
But its beauty was that time was beautiful, not now...

118
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:48,000
wele wî demî xweş bî... Na ... Şerîn pirnbî.
 
By God, that time was beautiful... Now... The sweet things
are gone.

119
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Bevre misahedek dikirin... Ewî devê cût sa ke cotî dewêre
 
They helped each other together... That time of plowing,
watch the plowing with cattle

120
00:06:53,000 --> 00:07:00,000
na haliye omrê min heftî salin sibê têgeredn hate evarî
havajî mezîna a ezî ...
 
now currently my age is seventy years, in the morning you
walk until the evening, that too is big, I...

121
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:08,000
e ji ne eczi. Xêr a? xwasa devareb bîceteya tu cût dojî
kufetêya tê rana xoxav dive tu nakî tê defte ne.
 
And not exhausted. What's good? it's nice, your cattle is by
your side, you're plowing, the tiredness gets up, it becomes
yourself, you don't do it, they put it away.

122
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Seyk ro re ser çuştê dibe. Etezonî
 
Watch, the sun goes over the peak. You know.

123
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
E...nako kîrpatore a rin a dkin
 
Yes... now they bring cultivators and do it.

124
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
dar berrr do go qî xera kiron
 
trees, watch, they ruined it all.

125
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Deta zane a rin zora zorda dibil kin verin wero nakir o xî
gî do xenje jere dor kûtike xo gev ale mane.
 
You know, now very forcefully they raise it up, they come in
without plowing, and all the rocks go down, the tree's roots
get exposed, all are left around.

126
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
yanî ne wakî e çaxeye kotî dewer o dar.
 
I mean, not like that time of plowing with cattle and trees.

127
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Bêlî... Em vagerên sa corete
 
Yes... Let's return to your work.

128
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:36,000
nako to pîşême birteştene catit bxobejin seri carexe denca
 
now you have many things in front of us, tell us about your
work yourself, then.

129
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:47,000
