Fîşka jî... vê dixistin di quncikê pexara da daxek yekê
xwa... pê fîşqê dikirin...
 
The wick too... they put it in the corner of the chimney and
pressed it on itself... they hit it with the wick...

242
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Di nav defxina da ava tebîr e ma ne... ti bîra ma nê. Em
gîştinê.
 
They blew it inside, it was a natural water... didn't you
remember. We reached it.

243
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:37,000
Em gîştinê erê?
 
We reached it, right?

244
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:42,000
Erê erê em giştin wan tiştan. Piştî lukus derket paşê çera
kahraba derketin.
 
Yes, yes, we reached those things. After the lukus came out,
then the electric lamps came out.

245
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Naha piraniya gundê we sobeyê êzinga ye, mazot wekî yê êzing
nîne? Piraniya yê êzing in.
 
Now, the majority of your village uses wood stoves, is
diesel not like wood? The majority are wood.

246
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Ji ber ko hemî dar li ba we hene... Ji berê da subê êzing
e... berê pexare bû. Ji pexarê jî naha dibînin sobeyê
êzingan.
 
Because you have all the trees with you... Wood stoves have
been used since the past... it used to be a chimney. From
the chimney they now see wood stoves.

247
00:16:54,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Naha taybet kîjan darê zêde têkeve? Zêtûn zêde dikeve? Û
darê...
 
Now especially which tree is used more? Is olive used more?
And tree...

248
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Zêtûn jî tê dikeve. Û darê sêv u gûzan... darê meşmiş,
behîv... hejîr, dev axara wa ye.
 
Olive is also used. And apple and walnut trees... apricot,
almond trees... fig, whatever comes to hand.

249
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Zêtûn e pir zêdetir e.
 
Olive is much more.

250
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Zêtûn û gûzan... Zêtûn e, meşmiş e, behîv e...
 
Olive and walnuts... It is olive, apricot, almond...

251
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Û da her malekê de sobeyê êzinga heye.
 
And in every house there is a wood stove.

252
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Her maleke da sobeyê êzinga heye.
 
In every house there is a wood stove.

253
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Te dî wek destpêkê sobeyê êzing çêkiriye ji cema Efrînê bû.
Wekî gundekî Tirmişa û bavê we pir nêzîk in.
 
You saw, as in the beginning, the wood stove was made from
Afrin gathering. Like the village of Tirmişa and your father
are very close.

254
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Erê, wan çêkir. Ev sobeyê êzingan...
 
Yes, they made it. This wood stove...

255
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:42,000
Piştî wê te dî bajarî jî çêkirin. Her kesî xwe sinyeta xwe
çêkiriye. Ne wisa kû pir çêkirin...
 
After that, you saw that the cities also made it. Everyone
made their own trays. It's not like they made a lot...

256
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Ka em silavekî bidin Hêysem jî, Hêysem jî em bipirsin...
 
Let's give a greeting to Hêysem too, let's ask Hêysem too...

257
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Hêysem jî em bipirsin.
 
Let's ask Hêysem too.

258
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Merheba ji te re jî, qewet be ji te re jî.
 
Hello to you too, power to you too.

259
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Hela û sehlen, bixêr hatin.
 
Welcome, welcome to you.

260
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Sax be. Welleh... wê wextê te ji xwe ra tîne sobê...
 
Be healthy. Well... that time you brought a stove for
yourself...

261
00:17:55,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Welleh koxî da zehmet e, serma ye... em tişt dikin naha
nakin, emê ji sermayê bimirin.
 
Well, working is hard. It's cold... we do things now, they
don't do them, we will die from the cold.

262
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Lê naha tu çend rojan e, tu ev êzinga hûr dikî?
 
But now, how many days have you been chopping this wood?

263
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Welleh teqrîben bûye sê çar rojan. Ev în da xistin û ev ne
